<title>USA: Pinkerton in Chilean steel joint venture.</title>
<headline>Pinkerton in Chilean steel joint venture.</headline>
<dateline>ENCINO, Calif 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pinkerton's Inc said it agreed to purchase 50 percent ownership in Steel S.A., a leading uniformed-officer security provider based in Santiago, Chile.  Terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>&quot;The Pinkerton-Steel joint venture will be a key part of our expansion over the next few years in the Latin American security market, Brown said.&quot;</p>
<p>Steel, established in 1991, is Chile's second-largest private security firm.  Its 1996 revenues were about $10.6 million in U.S. dollars.  Steel employs about 2,000 security officers deployed throughout Chile.</p>
</text>
